    "q-138484": {
      "dom_id": "step-q138484",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "For the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$",
      "worked_solution": "For an \"almost\" zero $m\\times n$ matrix with non-zero entries \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }_{1},\\,{\\sigma }_{2},\\,…,\\,{\\sigma }_{r}\n$$\n\non the main diagonal, the corresponding pseudoinverse is the \"almost\" zero $n\\times m$ matrix with entries \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }_{1}^{-1},\\,{\\sigma }_{2}^{-1},\\,…,\\,{\\sigma }_{r}^{-1}\n$$\n\non the main diagonal.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{+} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {4}^{-1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-138484-a",
